Z||000007||artherd||08-25-2001||03:55 PM||||Hey Tom, I actually really perfer my Rodney straight sport-shifter (I have the euro arm), it's great, I like the action of the straight arm, and surprisingly I have no trouble reaching it!  <P>It really all comes down to personal preference and what fits YOU, the driver, the best  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I suspect taller people would perfer the straight shifter, I'm 6'2" <P>I'd also like to move my steering wheel back about 20-30mm.<P>PS: the dash looks *Great!!*  How did you do it, where can we read all the details!?<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">   <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 08-25-2001).]||||reg||3
